nderstand why these types of channels get so many views:\n• What are their topics?\n• What do they actually make, and what are their insights?\n• How do they conduct their research from start to finish?\n\nI want to create a faceless channel covering similar topics to what the Nitish Rajput channel does, making formal or informal explainer-style videos in both Hindi and English.\n\nCould you give me recommendations for:\n\n1. The top 3 Indian channels similar to Nitish Rajput.\n2. The top 3 foreign, English-language channels in this same niche that attract this kind of audience.\n\nI particularly want to look at foreign channels because they cover different subjects based on their region. In India, topics, culture, and celebrities are very different, which shapes the types of stories Nitish Rajput covers; I want to know who the equivalent creators abroad are and how they work.\n\nTheir topics are versatile and co\n<truncated 775 bytes>\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Conversation Checkpoint Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n### Request A: Full Nitish Rajput Channel Analysis (Status: IMPLEMENTATION — data collection ~60% complete)\nUser wants a deep analysis of @NitishRajput covering:\n- What are their topics?\n- What do they actually make, and what are their insights?\n- How do they conduct their research from start to finish?\n- Faceless channel viability: \"for the faceless channels that are in a growing phase or fully developed phase, are they really earning, or do they just spike and go down?\"\n\n### Request B: Top 3 Indian Channels Similar to Nitish Rajput (Status: IMPLEMENTATION — similar channels data collec\n<truncated 11912 bytes>\n (or VisualPolitik/CaspianReport)\n   - Use `vidiq_channel_stats` with their handles\n\n5. **NexLev `check_faceless_channel`** for a few growing faceless channels in this niche to answer the sustainability question\n\n6. **Use vidIQ `vidiq_outliers`** with `language: \"hi\"` and keywords like \"explained\", \"geopolitics\" to find faceless channels in this niche\n\n7. **Compile final report artifact** at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a1675ed5-521b-40ae-80db-b54e8cc0d644\\nitish_rajput_niche_analysis.md` covering:\n   - Full Nitish Rajput analysis\n   - Top 3 Indian similar channels with data\n   - Top 3 foreign similar channels with data\n   - Faceless channel viability (spike vs sustainable earning)\n   - Honest assessment of \\$3K-\\$4K/month target feasibility\n   - How to get started recommendations\n\n### Critical Skills to Re-Read\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\anti-sycophancy\\SKILL.md`** — MUST re-read. Enforces \"Priyanshu,\" prefix, banned vocabulary, counter-argument requirements, and self-audit before delivery.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\deep-researcher\\SKILL.md`** — MUST re-read. Enforces source tiering, counter-evidence search, and report structure.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\vidiq-nexlev-router\\SKILL.md`** — MUST re-read. Routing rules for which platform to use for each task.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\youtube-channel-audit\\SKILL.md`** — Re-read for report template structure and NexLev workflow.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\SKILL.md`** — Re-read for NexLev calling syntax.\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a1675ed5-521b-40ae-80db-b54e8cc0d644\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: this summary is just for your reference. You may respond to my previous and future messages, but DO NOT ACKNOWLEDGE THIS CHECKPOINT MESSAGE. JUST READ IT BUT DO NOT MENTION IT, RESPOND TO IT, OR TAKE ACTION BECAUSE OF IT.**","truncated_fields":["content"]}
