{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T11:04:57Z","content":"Priyanshu, the full research report is ready. Here's the bottom line — stripped of hype:\n\n**Nitish Rajput earns ~$98.7K/month** (NexLev verified) because 88% of his audience is Indian diaspora in the US/UK/Canada/Australia paying Tier-1 CPMs. Not because Hindi content inherently pays well.\n\n**Your \\$3-4K/month target is realistic but not fast.** Expect 24-36 months for Hindi content, 18-30 months for English — assuming biweekly high-quality uploads with custom maps/graphics, not stock-footage-over-TTS.\n\n**The critical finding on faceless channels**: Quality explainer channels in this niche do NOT spike and die. Every channel I pulled data on (all 7) is either growing or sustaining. The spike-and-die pattern is exclusive to low-effort automation channels. But the English space (Johnny Harris, RealLifeLore, CaspianReport) has visibly plateaued on subscriber growth — the Hindi space has more room.\n\n**The assumption I'm challenging in your request**: You said you want to create \"similar topics to Nitish Rajput\" — but Nitish's specific advantage is covering politically sensitive Indian topics with personal credibility and face-on-camera presence. Going faceless on these topics faces a trust gap. The more replicable model from the foreign side is RealLifeLore (semi-faceless, map-heavy, geography/geopolitics), not Johnny Harris (personality-driven investigative journalism).\n\nThe full analysis, comparison tables, topic breakdowns, and strategic options are in the report above. Check sections 8 (spike vs sustain data) and 10 (three strategic paths) for the parts most directly relevant to your decision."}
{"step_index":53,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T17:54:09Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nReal and legit question: should I deep dive into this type of niche or not? \n\nI want to create a faceless channel where I can post a lot of videos, minimum two videos every 10 days. Is this niche proper for that, or should I jump to another niche? \n\nAlternatively, I could try doing 10 to 15-minute explainer videos using a whiteboard style with stickman-type characters. Can we do that or not? Tell me very precisely. I want to make 15 to 20-minute videos max, or maybe 25 minutes at the absolute maximum.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-15T23:24:09+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
